From 68c0de2b8d75d58f623bc626fc04513629a0c2f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:34:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] feat(backend): snapshots.csv, an index of a project's
 state snapshots

runtime_session.snapshot_index keeps <storage>/state_snapshots/<project>/snapshots.csv:
one row per snapshot, derived from its state.json, which stays the source of
truth. UTF-8 without BOM, a header, "\n" line ends, written with the csv module,
so comments with commas, quotes, line breaks or any script survive.

Columns (stable, documented in the module; new ones only ever at the end):
snapshot_id, captured_at_local, captured_at_utc, defective, comment,
environment_id, environment_name, session_id, control_mode, dataset_id,
joint_names, follower_joint_1..6, leader_joint_1..6 (empty unless
teleoperating), camera_names, camera_<n>_name/_color/_depth/_depth_preview for
the first four cameras (paths relative to the CSV), warnings.

Every change holds the project's lock (a thread lock, and flock on
snapshots.csv.lock across processes): a capture appends its row in one write
and fsyncs it; an edit rewrites the index from every state.json and renames it
into place. An index that is missing, has another header, a row of another
width, an id twice, no line end after its last row, or does not list every
snapshot exactly once is rebuilt the same way. state.json is written
atomically, so a rebuild never reads half of one.

